    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a daily registration limit on `POST /api/owners` that rejects creating an owner once 100 or more owners have already been registered today (by `registrationDate`), responding **429 Too Many Requests**. Following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing per-city capacity rule), I added:\n\n1. **`CheckDailyOwnerLimit.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today via `ownerRepository.findAll()` and throws when the count reaches 100.\n\n2. **`DailyOwnerLimitException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception so it routes through the escalation mechanism.\n\n3. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceptionHandler.java`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 responds `429` with an RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail`, matching the existing handler style.\n\n4. **`...DailyOwnerLimitException.yml`** (`officefloor/escalation/`) \u2014 binds the exception to the handler.\n\n5. Wired a new `checkDailyLimit` step into **`owners.POST.yml`**, placed after the city-capacity check and before `build` (so it runs as a validation guard before any entity construction/persistence).\n\nThe limit step runs before `build`, where new owners default their `registrationDate` to today, so the count correctly reflects owners created today. The target test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
